@startuml
title SFT transduction: input-predicate / output-term edges (`case_fold_sft`)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
  AttributeFontColor #111827
}

[*] --> q0

state "q0\naccepting" as q0 #EDE9FE

q0 --> q0 : [A-Z] / emit lowercase\n(Map c ↦ c+32)
q0 --> q0 : ¬[A-Z] / emit input\n(Identity)
q0 --> [*]

note right of q0
  Each edge carries a guard AND an
  output function: the guard `φ`
  decides WHETHER the edge fires;
  the output function `f` decides
  WHAT is emitted when it does.
  The two guards are complementary
  ([A-Z] ∧ ¬[A-Z] is unsatisfiable),
  so exactly one fires per element
  ⇒ the transducer is functional
  (single-valued).
end note

legend bottom
|= Color |= Element |
|<#EDE9FE> | symbolic transducer (SFT) state |
| φ / f | input guard `/` output function on an edge |
endlegend
@enduml
